v 3
d exactnl: Exact maximum likelihood estimation of the share-form nested logit
d
d Authors: Matthew J. Baker and Lisa M. George
d
d exactnl estimates the share-form nested logit demand model by exact
d maximum likelihood. The likelihood of the Berry (1994) log share-ratio
d includes a Jacobian term, (J-1)ln(1-sigma) per nest, that applied work
d omits. Because the term depends on the nesting parameter, omitting it
d biases within-group substitution estimates, and the bias is entangled
d with product counts when choice sets vary across markets. exactnl
d includes the term, requires no instrument for the within-nest share, and
d supports fixed-effect absorption, a control-function price instrument,
d and a direct product-count (crowding) term in mean utility.
d
d If you use this command, please cite:
d Baker, Matthew J. and Lisa M. George. 2026. Demand Estimation with
d Variable Choice Sets: A Likelihood Correction for Nested Logit.
d SSRN Working Paper 7207938. https://ssrn.com/abstract=7207938
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
